3354. Make Array Elements Equal to Zero

Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/make-array-elements-equal-to-zero/description/

Intuition 

1️ The process acts like a balance game — every time you hit a non-zero, you reduce it and reverse direction.
2️ Starting from a 0, you will keep bouncing left ↔ right and gradually reduce elements.
3️ For all elements to become 0, the total work on left and right must be balanced.
4️ Let left = sum of elements before index i, right = sum after i.
5️ If left == right → perfectly balanced → both directions (left & right) work → +2.
6️ If |left - right| == 1 → slight imbalance → only one direction works → +1.

Key Insight

This simulation problem reduces to checking balance of sums around a zero index, not actual movement.

Time Complexity (TC)
O(n)
One pass to compute total sum
One pass to check each index

Space Complexity (SC)
O(1)
Only using variables (sum, left, right, ans)


class Solution {
    public int countValidSelections(int[] nums) {
        int sum=0;
        for(int x:nums)sum+=x;
        int left=0;
        int ans=0;
        for(int i=0;i<nums.length;i++){
            left+=nums[i];
            int right=sum-left;
            if(nums[i]==0&& left==right)ans+=2;
            else if(nums[i]==0 && (Math.abs(left-right)==1))ans+=1;
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
